WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.540
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.880
- Welcome to Ear Biscuits, I'm Link.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.713
- And I'm Rhett.

00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:09.370
This week at the round
table of dim lighting

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.250
we are exploring the question,

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:16.250
what are our top 10 most
influential TV shows?

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.400
- Yeah so over the course of our lives,

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.662
we've watched our fair
share of television,

00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:24.969
and it's interesting 'cause I
started thinking about this,

00:00:24.969 --> 00:00:28.490
at certain pockets of
my life I was watching

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:30.451
a lot more television,

00:00:30.451 --> 00:00:33.940
and at other times less.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.100
And so, I think that my
list, which I have not shared

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.040
with you and you have not
shared your top 10 list with me.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.956
- That's what we're about
to do as a matter of fact.

00:00:42.956 --> 00:00:45.806
- Oh we're gonna do that and
share it with you, listener.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:51.650
It was really a truckin'
back down memory lane,

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.350
you know, and I was pleasantly surprised

00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:58.260
by the things that came
up when I started thinking

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.260
about television shows
that not only influenced me

00:01:03.898 --> 00:01:06.540
in terms of like my creative brain,

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.920
but also in terms of my
life, just personal impact.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:11.753
- [Rhett] Mm-hmm.

00:01:11.753 --> 00:01:15.480
- So this is not necessarily
our favorite television shows,

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.390
but it kind of is.

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:18.813
I have a lot of honorable mentions.

00:01:18.813 --> 00:01:20.630
- Well I would say most significant.

00:01:20.630 --> 00:01:22.563
I would be most significant in our lives.

00:01:22.563 --> 00:01:25.520
That's not as clear and
easy to say as influential.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.910
- Right, but this is not
what we believe to be

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:30.790
our top 10 best television
shows of all time.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:32.010
- No, not even close.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.700
- These are ones that we
have personal connections to

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.990
in one form or another
which we can flesh out

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:39.190
as we go through these things.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:42.380
- So while we did not share
the list with one another,

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:44.902
the one thing that we did do
just so you can understand

00:01:44.902 --> 00:01:49.730
the exercise is that
we did tell each other

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:54.244
that we would be going
back through our lives,

00:01:54.244 --> 00:01:58.880
so it was kinda going back
to the first television shows

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.970
you could remember being significant

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:04.800
and then I kinda just, I
went through my entire life--

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.040
- Okay.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.540
I didn't do it that way but--

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.809
- That's, what I'm saying
is, just to give you an idea

00:02:09.809 --> 00:02:11.210
where they come from.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:14.740
Some are gonna be when we were
kids, some are more recent.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:15.610
Not too many.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:17.120
- All of mine are current.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.400
No just kidding.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:23.400
But the reason why I thought
to have this conversation was

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.410
because something happened over the break

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.357
that I chose not to share with
you a couple of weeks back

00:02:28.357 --> 00:02:32.697
when I was giving my
update on the holiday break

00:02:32.697 --> 00:02:34.830
and my family time.
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:39.260
- And when I went to Sedona so
the thing I didn't tell you,

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.040
something very special happened

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.435
that our family bonded over something

00:02:44.435 --> 00:02:49.435
and it was the reality competition
show known as Survivor.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.569
Have you heard of this show?

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:54.160
- This is a little weird.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.810
- It is a little weird, isn't it?

00:02:56.773 --> 00:03:01.773
But it turns out Survivor
became a very special part

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:04.980
of my family's holiday break

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.790
in a very unanticipated
bonding experience.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.270
- You know, whatever it
takes, man. (chuckles)

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.930
- Exactly.
- Whatever it takes

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:15.337
to get everybody together.
- Exactly.

00:03:15.337 --> 00:03:19.120
And a magical thing happened,
but a little back story.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.200
When we were on tour in Australia,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.810
we went back to our rooms.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.721
When we were in Sydney, we were
in that high rise apartment.

00:03:25.721 --> 00:03:28.450
- Yeah, high livin'.
- Towards the end of that,

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:30.630
the Sydney part of the trip,
there was this one night

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:32.130
where we were like, let's just order in.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.530
You kinda get to a point in
your trip where you're like,

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.860
I just don't think we can
mobilize everybody to go out

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:41.470
to eat again and I feel a little over it,

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:44.670
so we just stayed in the
room and ordered pizza.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.680
And I put on the
television, I was like hey,

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.240
let's watch some Australian television.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.120
You had been talking about
how nice everybody was.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.530
You were learning a lot about the culture.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:53.363
- I was.

00:03:53.363 --> 00:03:54.779
Very, very nice.
- I was like, well,

00:03:54.779 --> 00:03:57.310
the Neals need to do that
too so we turned it on

00:03:57.310 --> 00:04:00.770
and it was the Australian
version of Survivor

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:03.090
just happened to be on and I'm like,

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.410
kids, this is, look at
this, it's Survivor.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:06.430
And they're like, what?

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:11.430
And I was like, well it's
basically a game show.

00:04:12.597 --> 00:04:14.560
It's a reality competition show.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:16.793
Basically, I was having trouble.

00:04:18.526 --> 00:04:21.900
American Idol and The Voice
are reality competition shows

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.130
where people sing but it turns
out that these other ones

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.700
where they take a group of
people and they just strand 'em

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.220
out on an island or something.

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:29.053
- They had never heard of this concept?

00:04:29.053 --> 00:04:31.650
- They had never heard
of Survivor at any point.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.540
- I would have thought that
Survivor was like in memes

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.013
or something, in some way.

00:04:35.013 --> 00:04:36.587
There's some way kids
find out about things.

00:04:36.587 --> 00:04:40.670
- I just don't think it's cool
enough for that. (chuckles)

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.840
I couldn't have told you that
Survivor was still going on

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:43.673
but lo and behold here it was,

00:04:43.673 --> 00:04:46.540
and this was the Australian
version of Survivor

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:51.084
but it happened to be an episode
where they were bringing in

00:04:51.084 --> 00:04:54.790
I think heroes and villains
from previous Survivors.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:56.422
- Oh they're already there
in Australia as well.

00:04:56.422 --> 00:04:59.100
- Well one of the guys was from America,

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:00.970
a famous guy who I won't mention

00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:02.570
'cause I can't remember his
name but he's from another--

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.490
- Are Americans as cool to Australians

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.330
as Australians are to America?

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:08.250
Could you sense that in the
way that they set him up?

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.520
- It was one of the first
episodes of the season

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.480
and they voted the guy off so
I'll put it to you that way.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:14.360
- Okay apparently not.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:17.000
So apparently you have a correct
understanding of Americans.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.210
- But I was like, oh, you
don't know about Survivor

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:20.370
so we just started watching it.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.040
We just watched the one
episode out of context

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.420
and everybody, I just made a mental note,

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.810
everybody seemed to be into it.

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:27.900
- Yeah.
- They're asking questions

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.800
about how Survivor works as
a game and stuff like that

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.647
so I just made a mental note,
got back to the States--

00:05:33.528 --> 00:05:36.375
- Jeff Probst was not involved.

00:05:36.375 --> 00:05:37.690
- No.
- Directly.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:39.091
- No he was not hosting.

00:05:39.091 --> 00:05:41.350
He was not directly involved.

00:05:41.350 --> 00:05:42.523
I get back here, we're like,

00:05:42.523 --> 00:05:46.590
we're filming a couple
weeks ago and I think Kevin

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:50.280
brought up something about
Survivor and I was like,

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.700
hold on, were you just
talking about Survivor?

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:55.520
And he was like, yeah John
and I are big Survivor fans.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.700
If you see the two of us,
or maybe somebody else,

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.890
trying to, if you see
the two of them together,

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:01.690
I can guarantee they're
talking about Survivor

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:04.724
and I was like, I would
have laughed at you--

00:06:04.724 --> 00:06:06.150
- Two weeks ago.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:08.150
- Before my Australian
trip but the funny thing

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:11.056
that happened and I told him
the story, and they were like.

00:06:11.056 --> 00:06:14.616
I was like, I think we should
start watching Survivor.

00:06:14.616 --> 00:06:16.150
I think my family would be into it.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:19.340
He was like, oh, you definitely should.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:22.830
It's amazing, and they're
getting both into it

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:25.470
and I'm like you guys are
dorks, but okay, whatever.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.303
- Yeah definitely.

00:06:26.303 --> 00:06:29.100
- And they said you should watch the

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:32.710
Millennials vs. Gen X
season which was like

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:35.590
three seasons ago so pretty recent.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:37.370
- It's still going.
- Said it's really good.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.850
There's like 400 seasons of this thing.

00:06:40.850 --> 00:06:43.430
No literally I think
there's like 36 seasons.

00:06:43.430 --> 00:06:45.150
It is still going.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:46.640
I didn't even know it.
- Twice a year

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:47.930
for almost 20 years I guess.

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:52.390
- So the week leading up to our trip,

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:54.561
the kids are getting out of school,

00:06:54.561 --> 00:06:55.831
school work's dying down,

00:06:55.831 --> 00:06:59.270
I start putting on the Survivor
and everybody gets into it.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:02.764
Like every single member of the family.

00:07:02.764 --> 00:07:06.286
It's so hard to pick out a
movie or a television show

00:07:06.286 --> 00:07:09.223
that everybody can get into.

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:13.360
But Lando loved it because
it was like adventurous

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:17.331
and outdoors and oh, that
one's in Fiji where we went.

00:07:17.331 --> 00:07:18.970
- Right.
- So I was like,

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:22.160
we been to Fiji, we've experienced kinda,

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.023
well we were like at a resort.

00:07:23.023 --> 00:07:25.410
They're not at a resort.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:27.350
- Not exactly the same thing.

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:31.350
- Lincoln, he loves strategy games.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.470
He loves strategy so he's into that.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:37.380
Lily really enjoyed the
humor of kinda laughing

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.860
at these people basically
becoming characters.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:43.100
And Christy really enjoyed all of it.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:44.520
I don't know exactly what Christy loved

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.730
but I think--
- She likes the guys

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:47.563
with the shirts off.

00:07:47.563 --> 00:07:50.010
- Guys with the shirts
off, there was a model.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:52.520
A male model.
- Of course she does.

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:54.177
- And--
- Survivor body they call it.

00:07:54.177 --> 00:07:57.423
- And I liked the production.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.158
I would pause Survivor and I would say,

00:08:01.158 --> 00:08:04.540
"Guys, do you see how
brilliant the production is?"

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.980
Rhett, they have it down, I
know this sounds ludicrous--

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:09.940
- No no no.
- They have it down

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:12.200
to a science.
- What's ludicrous is pausing

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.840
and explaining it to your family.

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:16.410
Appreciating it, no I am
totally on the same page.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:18.290
- I was just overflowing with joy.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:20.724
- It's a production wonder
but we've talked about this,

00:08:20.724 --> 00:08:22.393
in fact, we've talked about
this very specifically--

00:08:22.393 --> 00:08:24.470
- It's that Dad thing.
- You can't be the,

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:26.290
I do the same thing, you cannot be the dad

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.820
who makes your family stop

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:29.810
and acknowledge how awesome something is

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.130
because you think it's awesome.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:33.850
You have to just give it to
'em and let them experience it

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:35.343
on their own terms.

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.950
No more pausing.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.460
- They each had their
thing but I was trying

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:40.945
to get them to appreciate
what I appreciate

00:08:40.945 --> 00:08:44.113
which was after all of these seasons,

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:49.100
they've got, I mean, the contestants,

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.910
some of them are obsessed
with game player Survivor

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.020
so they're really good at
it and they invent new ways

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:56.564
to play it and new strategies come out,

00:08:56.564 --> 00:08:59.590
but the way that they present
it in terms of the editing

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:04.590
and they bring story out and
you have these character arcs

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:09.800
is masterful, I mean it really
is amazing to me. (chuckles)

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:14.820
And so it's, I might have to alter my list

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.210
and put Survivor on there.

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.620
It is an honorable--
- So hold on.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:20.400
You're saying Survivor
is not, after all this,

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.237
Survivor is not on your list?

00:09:22.237 --> 00:09:24.312
- (chuckles) It should be now because

00:09:24.312 --> 00:09:26.760
it just seems so fresh, I
don't know if it's gonna stand

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:30.520
the test of time 'cause
every night at Sedona

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:32.540
we would do hiking and
everything I talked about

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:35.460
but then we would also be
talking about Survivor.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.430
We had something that everybody
could talk about together

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.650
during the day and then
at night we'd be like,

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:43.502
hey let's all get all in our
PJs and let's make some popcorn

00:09:43.502 --> 00:09:46.070
and let's sit down and
have our Survivor session.

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:49.340
Like everybody was into it,
and while we were hiking,

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:54.340
Christy and I were like wow,
this is a rare gem of a moment.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.900
Thank you Jeff Probst.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:10:00.894
- And so are you, how much
do you watch in a sitting?

00:10:00.894 --> 00:10:04.010
- We would watch two or three episodes.

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:05.920
- Wow.
- In a sitting.

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:08.210
And so we finished it the night before

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:11.310
we were leaving Sedona and they were like

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:12.710
let's watch another one.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.380
So we're out to dinner and I'm googling

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:17.760
what are the best seasons of Survivor?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:21.118
There's this very involved Reddit thread,

00:10:21.118 --> 00:10:23.666
a Survivor Reddit thread
where people talk about

00:10:23.666 --> 00:10:26.550
what are the best seasons
and which ones to watch

00:10:26.550 --> 00:10:28.520
and this one's the best but you have

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:31.180
to watch this one before
because it spoils something

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:35.130
about the strategy so,
I figured all that out

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:37.320
and we're like we're gonna watch China,

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.810
and so we come back and we
start watching it and I'm like--

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:41.710
- What are you watching
it on, what platform?

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:43.300
- A laptop.

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:44.890
- No what platform?

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:46.480
- Like a coffee table?

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:47.810
No I'm messing with you.

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:49.500
Hulu.

00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:51.560
Hulu has Survivor, all of 'em.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:53.150
- Okay.

00:10:53.150 --> 00:10:57.120
- And I immediately notice,
people are gushing about

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:59.077
how great this season is.

00:10:59.077 --> 00:11:00.523
I never watched it.

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:04.344
The only season I had
watched was, Christy and I,

00:11:04.344 --> 00:11:08.780
like in our second year of
marriage we watched season three

00:11:08.780 --> 00:11:11.820
Survivor: Outback Australia
and there was a goat farmer.

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:12.657
He was very funny.

00:11:12.657 --> 00:11:13.553
That's the only season we watched.

00:11:13.553 --> 00:11:18.553
- And I think that it was, it
was a phenomenon at that time.

00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:21.350
Jessie and I watched multiple seasons.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:24.487
It was appointment television.
- Yeah season two was like

00:11:24.487 --> 00:11:26.153
the number one show on television.

00:11:26.153 --> 00:11:27.458
- I remember when it came out--

00:11:27.458 --> 00:11:29.962
- But I didn't watch that one.
- Just thinking it was like,

00:11:29.962 --> 00:11:32.782
this is changing everything!

00:11:32.782 --> 00:11:34.990
- Yeah.
- And we had to watch it.

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:36.290
And then I don't remember what happened.

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:38.500
- Reality competition shows
really became mainstream.

