- So that was from 1993 to 1998.

00:36:27.740 --> 00:36:29.645
I remember watching it after school.

00:36:29.645 --> 00:36:30.530
- Yep.

00:36:30.530 --> 00:36:32.650
- I don't know that I
could have articulated it.

00:36:32.650 --> 00:36:35.360
I guess I would have to.

00:36:35.360 --> 00:36:36.320
It was the humor,

00:36:36.320 --> 00:36:38.020
I mean it was--
- So specific.

00:36:38.020 --> 00:36:41.852
- Absolutely the specific jokes.

00:36:41.852 --> 00:36:45.260
I mean like Pinky and the Brain I'm gonna,

00:36:45.260 --> 00:36:47.980
it had its own spin-off show later

00:36:47.980 --> 00:36:52.980
which I've never actually
watched, but that was gold.

00:36:53.480 --> 00:36:58.480
And then the way that
the Animaniacs would,

00:36:58.520 --> 00:37:01.017
they would, I think there was innuendo.

00:37:01.017 --> 00:37:05.180
It was all types of, I
mean it was very joke-heavy

00:37:05.180 --> 00:37:07.080
and it was very, there
was a lot of winking

00:37:07.080 --> 00:37:09.077
at the older audience.
- You felt--

00:37:09.077 --> 00:37:12.400
- And I was just old enough
to know that was happening.

00:37:12.400 --> 00:37:14.380
- Yeah you felt like you were, well,

00:37:14.380 --> 00:37:16.540
I'm sure there was other things obviously,

00:37:16.540 --> 00:37:18.763
The Simpsons which did not make my list,

00:37:20.038 --> 00:37:22.210
was happening around the same time,

00:37:22.210 --> 00:37:26.682
but something about the darkness

00:37:26.682 --> 00:37:31.682
and the weirdness that was
the Animaniacs world view,

00:37:33.720 --> 00:37:34.913
and the way that they saw things

00:37:34.913 --> 00:37:36.527
and the way that they pointed out things

00:37:36.527 --> 00:37:38.460
and the way that they talked about things,

00:37:38.460 --> 00:37:42.603
it was a little bit of that
old school Warner Brothers,

00:37:44.307 --> 00:37:47.340
you know, crazy physical thing

00:37:47.340 --> 00:37:52.340
but then it brought this second
layer of smart, dark humor.

00:37:53.790 --> 00:37:57.610
It was subversive and it was
hitting exactly the right time,

00:37:57.610 --> 00:38:01.710
in 93 to 98 so I was watching
it basically in high school,

00:38:01.710 --> 00:38:04.573
like you said and at that time,

00:38:04.573 --> 00:38:06.560
because by the time you're in high school,

00:38:06.560 --> 00:38:09.768
schedules get crazy, it
would come on after school

00:38:09.768 --> 00:38:12.105
and so it was one of those things that

00:38:12.105 --> 00:38:16.280
I didn't always see
but I never didn't stop

00:38:16.280 --> 00:38:17.885
and watch it if it was on.

00:38:17.885 --> 00:38:21.818
And yeah, again, to me,

00:38:21.818 --> 00:38:25.110
it made the list because of how

00:38:26.072 --> 00:38:27.310
it was revolutionary.

00:38:27.310 --> 00:38:30.060
I think most of the
things in the list for me

00:38:30.060 --> 00:38:32.327
were revolutionary in their own right

00:38:32.327 --> 00:38:35.103
and that's what made them
revolutionary in my own life.

00:38:35.103 --> 00:38:37.660
- I think it would be higher on my list

00:38:39.180 --> 00:38:44.180
if I would have moved onto
watching other animated comedies,

00:38:44.320 --> 00:38:45.930
which now is its own genre.

00:38:45.930 --> 00:38:50.000
I mean you talk about you got
the whole Adult Swim of it all

00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:54.570
and I mean, yeah, The Simpsons
obviously didn't make my list

00:38:54.570 --> 00:38:58.570
because I'm still embarrassed
to say I've never watched

00:38:58.570 --> 00:39:00.050
a complete episode of The Simpsons.

00:39:00.050 --> 00:39:01.600
It was one of those things that

00:39:03.970 --> 00:39:06.470
I think I was, at a young age I was told

00:39:06.470 --> 00:39:07.560
you're not supposed to watch it.

00:39:07.560 --> 00:39:08.393
- We weren't allowed to watch it--

00:39:08.393 --> 00:39:09.535
- We weren't allowed to watch it--

00:39:09.535 --> 00:39:11.243
- When it was happening.

00:39:11.243 --> 00:39:12.950
Early years.
- Early years

00:39:12.950 --> 00:39:17.720
and then I just wasn't a subversive kid

00:39:17.720 --> 00:39:19.510
so whenever I was told
not to do something,

00:39:19.510 --> 00:39:21.560
then I'd just think, I
said oh, I guess that means

00:39:21.560 --> 00:39:24.710
all the way into forever
when the show is like

00:39:24.710 --> 00:39:28.840
the most amazing show in
the history of television,

00:39:28.840 --> 00:39:30.620
not just animation.

00:39:30.620 --> 00:39:34.842
The longest running, I don't
know what the record is, but--

00:39:34.842 --> 00:39:36.050
- And I've seen The Simpsons.

00:39:36.050 --> 00:39:38.300
The reason it didn't
make my list is because,

00:39:39.618 --> 00:39:42.870
it didn't influence me,
it wasn't as impactful.

00:39:42.870 --> 00:39:46.440
